  "summary_en": "Egypt's National Council for AI issues voluntary responsible-AI guidelines (v1.0, 2023), adapting OECD, UNESCO and EU approaches. It sets general and implementation guidelines covering transparency, fairness, human oversight, accountability, risk management and impact assessment, and states that AI should not have legal personality.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Users have a right to know when interacting with AI rather than a human.",
   "AI systems must not be given legal personality; accountability lies with natural or legal persons.",
   "Final human determination must always be in place, with ability to modify, stop or retire the system.",
   "Government AI projects require a prior impact assessment and MCIT supervision.",
   "Foreign AI products must follow the guidelines and use locally relevant data; guidelines reviewed annually with public consultation."
